 "intro_html": "A celebration dish: beef short ribs braised until they come away from the bone, in a <b>sweet-savoury soy sauce softened with grated pear</b>, with chunks of radish and carrot, shiitake and chestnuts. Completely mild. In Turkey ask for <b>kaburga</b> cut into <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"5\" data-s=\"0\">5 cm</span> pieces. It works in a <b>steel sauté pan with a tight-fitting lid</b> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"28\" data-s=\"0\">28 cm</span>) on low heat. Turn the ribs a few times and keep some hot water nearby, because a wide pan loses more liquid than a pot. This is a home adaptation built from several Korean sources and has not been kitchen tested.",
