 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Put the ribs in a large bowl of cold water for <b>30–60 minutes</b> to draw out blood, changing the water once. Soak the dried shiitake in warm water at the same time.</li><li>Trim off thick outer pieces of fat. Make 2–3 shallow cuts along the meat of each rib so the sauce gets in.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Soak and trim the ribs",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [],
    "illustration": "illustrations/galbi-jjim/1.webp?v=15a1e8de3b",
    "photo": null,
    "result": null,
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 1,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~45 min, mostly soaking",
   "time_html": "<span>~45 min, mostly soaking</span>",
   "title": "Soak and trim the ribs",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"kg\" data-a=\"1\">1 kg</span>",
     "name_html": "Beef short ribs (kaburga), cut 5 cm"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"4\" data-n=\"1\">4</span>",
     "name_html": "Dried shiitake"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Fill the sauté pan halfway with water and bring it to a boil. Add the drained ribs and boil for <b>5 minutes</b>; grey scum will rise.</li><li>Drain the ribs into a colander and rinse each one under warm water. Wash out the pan. This makes the sauce clean and glossy instead of murky.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "high",
    "label_html": "<span>high</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Blanch the ribs in the pan",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Rinse each blanched rib",
      "src": "illustrations/galbi-jjim/2-how1.webp?v=a6f2bcf1e7"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/galbi-jjim/2.webp?v=294872eed6",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~10 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~10 min</span>",
   "title": "Blanch the ribs in the pan",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"kg\" data-a=\"1\">1 kg</span>",
     "name_html": "Beef short ribs (kaburga), cut 5 cm"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Grate the pear and onion on the fine side of the grater and mince the garlic. Stir them into the soy sauce, sugar, honey, ginger, pepper and sesame oil.</li><li>Put the ribs back into the clean pan in one layer, pour over the sauce and the <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"600\" data-s=\"0\">600 ml</span> water and bring to a boil. Cover, lower to <b>low</b> and braise at a gentle bubble for <b>1 hour</b>.</li><li>Turn the ribs every 20 minutes. The liquid should stay at least halfway up the ribs; top up with hot water if it drops lower.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "boil, then low",
    "label_html": "<span>boil, then low</span>",
    "off": false
   },
